# The shared entries of an account dir that CARRY DATA other accounts read:
# transcripts and auto-memory (projects), plugins, skills, hooks and the
# user-level CLAUDE.md. One name per line; a line starting with `#` is a comment.
#
# ONE DEFINITION, two readers, so they cannot disagree about what a split is:
#   scripts/claude-account-dirs.sh  a REAL directory at one of these names is a
#                                   split (REAL-DIR, --check exits 1, verify-tools
#                                   FAILs, the first prompt warns); a real
#                                   directory at any OTHER shared name is
#                                   LOCAL-DIR, informational
#   zsh/functions/claude.sh         claude-doctor's pooled-sharing invariant
#
# Why a list rather than "every directory": Claude Code makes some directories
# per config dir (state/, telemetry/, chrome/ are real in account dirs today).
# One session on the shared ~/.claude (CLAUDE_ISOLATION_OFF=1, the wrapper's
# fallback, `command claude`, an IDE extension) creates the same names there,
# and every account dir would then read as split, permanently, over empty dirs.
projects
plugins
skills
hooks
CLAUDE.md
